cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the protocol version you used, not the repository as a whole. If you used the harness only, cite the software release."
title: "BendEDA: Evaluating Bend 2 Laws and Proof Gates in Agentic Electronic Design Automation"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered, fully digital and fully public study of whether Bend 2's
  laws-and-proofs workflow improves the trustworthiness of agent-written
  hardware designs, measured against a hidden oracle and against an equivalent
  locked SystemVerilog Assertion specification. No human authors the Bend 2
  laws: law, model, reference-proof and oracle artifacts are produced by
  separately scoped agents under Freebuff control, with separation of duties
  enforced by sandboxes, hash locks and provenance records.
